d0cb6783-b927-4b88-86b0-5894b1264e28.pdf	The document discusses system security in the context of electronic commerce. It covers security requirements such as confidentiality, integrity, availability, and non-repudiation. It explores authentication methods including passwords, challenge-response systems, biometrics, and multi-factor authentication. Common attacks, like snooping, modification, masquerading, and denial of service, are also described. Finally, the document discusses Access Control like Discretionary Access Control (DAC) and Bell-LaPadula model.	application/pdf	9	t	This document covers system security in electronic commerce, detailing security requirements (confidentiality, integrity, availability, non-repudiation), policies, and mechanisms. It discusses security threats, common attacks (snooping, modification, masquerading, denial of service, malicious code, viruses, worms), and defense strategies. The document delves into authentication methods (passwords, challenge-response, biometrics, multi-factor) and access control models (DAC, MAC, access control matrix, ACL, capabilities list, Bell-LaPadula model) to ensure secure system operation.	056281f1-26dc-42d3-a13e-4e861451fc42		University of Science	[0.036330145,0.052760694,-0.004181805,0.00064097217,0.028238432,-0.037703667,-0.038171366,-0.015952125,0.03957718,0.017612452,0.0047718,0.026751595,0.119896844,0.04875074,-0.029750368,-0.056032408,0.02852313,-0.043081135,0.0040065744,-0.0021528022,0.037257235,-0.024571588,0.039192855,-0.008688468,0.015010145,-0.018393092,0.010470999,0.038287584,-0.046419375,0.035798844,0.03580898,-0.07477434,0.0047497978,0.0507394,0.010291165,0.01211065,-0.024937456,-0.031077785,0.0044779875,0.05369502,0.017720925,0.054396804,0.029162474,-0.031434003,0.016945101,-0.035456132,0.024647834,0.0168067,-0.023784256,-0.009710183,0.03858767,0.018749533,0.049154084,0.030424677,-0.03634704,-0.018637128,0.015165207,0.029231248,-0.040447876,0.028708374,-0.035237223,0.0075473716,-0.04724