938522,0.0017002051,-0.058292348,-0.037773572,-0.049467597,-0.028467568,-0.0013250451,0.022737134,-0.018960793,0.04128524,-0.019594144,-0.016744738,0.0018046414,0.009549832,0.019711228,-0.02662662,-0.030598223,0.057535354,-0.004835437,0.0173683,0.03627695,-0.0062232884,0.013630456,0.040083326,0.015279316,0.077712774,-0.056802887,-0.017342677,0.05927331,-0.040816043,0.013782211,0.008007777,-0.023367744,0.013453317,0.0140528055,-0.04187272,-0.06933913,-0.008589135,-0.015544785,-0.0066412054,0.047431733,0.049343895,0.020133082,-0.002561832,0.022655116,-0.010132823,-0.041385993,0.047698647,0.047722094,0.015877256,0.011243961,-0.022465127,-0.007854188,0.007477256,0.050764788,-0.036115248,0.03770064,0.04481618,0.016179685,0.0055893776,-0.029243462,0.06373701,-0.04425319,-0.02937934,0.034697317]	Multimodal for Sentiment Analysis\nDr. Bui Thanh Hung\nData Science Laboratory\nData Science Department, Faculty of Information Technology Industrial University of Ho Chi Minh city\nbuithanhhung@iuh.edu.vn\n1- Introduction\n2- Related Work\n3- Proposed Method\n4- Experiment\n5- Conclusion\nWhat is multimodal?\n✓In our case, focusing on NLP: text + one or more other modality (images, speech, audio, olfaction, others).\n✓We’ll mostly focus on images as the other modality.\n✓Why does multimodality matter?\nMultimodal\nLab\nA range of very good reasons:\n▪ Faithfulness: Human experience is multimodal\n▪ Practical: The internet & many applications multimodal are\n▪ Data efficiency and availability:\n✓Efficiency: Multimodal data is rich and “high bandwidth” (compared to language; quoting LeCun, “an imperfect, incomplete, and low-bandwidth serialization protocol for the internal data structures we call thoughts”), so better for learning?\n✓Scaling: More data is better, and we’re running out of high quality text data. 6\nMultimodality is one of the main frontiers of the new foundation model revolution.\nMultimodal applications\nLet’s say we’re dealing with two modalities – text, and images:\n▪ Retrieval (image <> text)\n▪ Captioning (image -> text)\n▪ Generation (text -> image)\n▪ Visual question answering (image + text -> text)\n▪ Multimodal classification (image + text -> label)\n▪ Better understanding/generation (image+text -> label/text)\nProblems with multimodality\nIf it’s so important, why isn’t every system multimodal from first principles?\n✓One modality can dominate other modalities.\n✓Additional modalities can add noise.\n✓Full coverage over modalities is not guaranteed.\n✓We are (were) not ready.\n✓It’s complicated.\nMultimodal\nMultimodal foundation models\nLab\n1- Introduction\nD\nS\nLab\n1- Introduction\nD\nS\nLab\n1- Introduction\nD\nS\n1- Introduction\nLab\nLab\n1- Introduction\nHillary Clinton ~\nDemocratic Party\nMentions\nTotal\nNo. of positive\nNo. of negative\nNo. of neutral\n785\n151\n155\n479\nDonald Trump ~\nRepublican Party\n\n\n=== [BẢNG SỐ LIỆU] ===\nMentions 1412 Total 255 No. of positive 402 No. of negative 755 No. of neutral\n======================\nWhat is Sentiment Analysis?\nSentiment analysis (SA) or opinion mining\n✓ computational study of opinion, sentiment, appraisal, evaluation, and emotion.\nWhy is it important?\n✓ Opinions are key influencers of our behaviors.\n✓ Rise of AI and chatbots\n• Emotion and sentiment are key to human communication\nSentiment Analysis on Text\nLove the sunset. The view is so beautiful here…\nSentiment Analysis on Image\n2- Related Work\nSentiment Analysis on multimodel: Text & Image\nThis is unbelievable\nThis is unbelievable\n+\n+\n|\nD\nS\nLab\nSentiment Analysis on Text\n✓ Rehman, Anwar Ur & Malik, Ahmad & Raza, Basit & Ali, Waqar. (2019). A Hybrid CNN-LSTM Model for Improving Accuracy of Movie Reviews Sentiment Analysis. Multimedia Tools and Applications.\n✓ Bui Thanh Hung. (2019) Domain-Specific Versus General-Purpose Word Representations in Sentiment Analysis for Deep Learning Models. Frontiers in Intelligent Computing: Theory and Applications pp 252- 264, Springer.\n2- Related Work\nSentiment Analysis on Image\n✓ You, Quanzeng et al. “Visual Sentiment Analysis by Attending on Local Image Regions.” AAAI (2017).\n✓ Al-Ghalibi, Maha et al. “Deep Attention Learning Mechanisms for Social Media Sentiment Image Revelation.” International Journal of Computer and Communication Engineering 9 (2020): 1-17.\n✓ Chandrasekaran et al. (2022). Visual Sentiment Analysis Using Deep Learning Models with Social Media Data. Applied Sciences.\nSentiment Analysis on multimodel: Text & Image\n✓ Gaspar, António & Alexandre, Luís. (2019). A Multimodal Approach to Image Sentiment Analysis, Intelligent Data Engineering and Automated Learning – IDEAL 2019, Cham: Springer International Publishing 2019\n✓ Yadav, Ashima & Vishwakarma, Dinesh. (2022). A Deep Multi-Level Attentive network for Multimodal Sentiment Analysis. ACM Transactions on Multimedia Computing, Communications, and Applications.\n2- Related Work\nOur Solution\n✓Solving the sentiment analysis problem on Image & Text\n✓Proposing three fusion methods to solve the sentiment analysis problem on multi data models.\n✓Combining text features with enhanced features\n✓Experiment with various pre-trained CNN models to extract image features to find the optimal feature\nS\n3- Proposed Model\nLab\nFeature of Sentiment Analysis on Text\n• Preprocessing Text\n• Extracting Feature using pre-trained BERT-base mode and taking the vector of token [CLS] at the last layer\nSentiment Analysis on Text\nEnhanced Features of Text\nFeature of Sentiment Analysis on Image\n• Preprocessing Image\n• Extracting Feature using pre-trained DenseNet201 and taking the output vector of the last hidden layer\nSentiment Analysis on Image\nD\nS\n3- Proposed Model\nLab\nFusion Approach\nD\nS\nLab\n3- Proposed Model\nFusion Approach\nIntermediate Fusion\n• Combine text and image features\n• Self-attention to learn important information in association feature\n• The softmax performs the classification\nD\nS\nLab\n3- Proposed Model\nFusion Approach\nLate Fusion\n• Classify separately with 2 features: Text and Image\n• Caculate weighted average on 2 outputs to get the final classification result\nD\nS\nLab\n3- Proposed Model\nFusion Approach\nHybrid Fusion\n• Combine Intermediate Fusion và Late Fusion\n• Classify separately with 3 features: Text, Image and Mix\n• Caculate weighted average on 3 outputs to get the final classification result\nDataset\nMVSA-Single & MVSA-Multiple\n• Includes pairs of text and image data collected from Twitter posts\n• Text and image data has its own label\n• There are 3 labels: positive, negative and neutral\nDataset\nText and image data has its own label\n⇒ Combine to one label\nD\n4- Experiment\nDataset: Rule to combine the label\nSame\n® {\nTwo labels are opposite\n©6 !\nDataset\nDataset\nTrain, Val and Test using the SMOTE algorithm\nToolkits\nPython version 3.7\nLib:\n• Tensorflow Keras: CNN\n• Transformer: BERT\n• OpenCV: Image preprocessing\n• nltk: POS tagging và Named-Entity-Recognition\n• plotly: visualization\nEvaluation\nS\nLab\n4- Experiment\nResult Sentiment Analysis on Text\nResult Sentiment Analysis on Text\n\n\n=== [BẢNG SỐ LIỆU] ===\nMVSA-Single Đặc trưng Accuracy GloVe 0.521 BERT + LSTM 0.623 BERT + POS + LSTM 0.632 BERT + POS + NER + LSTM 0.621 F1-score 0.433 0.632 0.637 0.635 MVSA-Multiple Accuracy F1-score 0.431 0.419 0.668 0.633 0.660 0.627 0.667 0.630\n======================\nD\nS\n4- Experiment\nLab\nD\nS\nLab\nResult Sentiment Analysis on Image\n\n\n=== [BẢNG SỐ LIỆU] ===\nMVSA-Single Đặc trưng Accuracy F1-score Xception 0.603 0.607 VGG16 0.612 0.596 VGG19 0.623 0.585 ResNet50 0.543 0.432 ResNet101 0.481 0.413 ResNet152 0.510 0.425 DenseNet121 0.559 0.558 DenseNet169 0.599 0.604 DenseNet201 0.630 0.625 MVSA-Multiple Accuracy F1-score 0.596 0.557 0.571 0.541 0.595 0.541 0.566 0.518 0.569 0.520 0.568 0.518 0.608 0.534 0.602 0.532 0.580 0.570 45\n======================\nD\nS\nLab\nResult Sentiment Analysis on multimodel: Image & Text\nS\n4- Experiment\nLab\nResult Sentiment Analysis on multimodel: Image & Text\nD\nS\n4- Experiment\nLab\nResult\nSentiment Analysis on multimodel: Image & Text\n\n\n=== [BẢNG SỐ LIỆU] ===\nMô hình Accuracy F1-score Image 0.623 0.624 Text 0.623 0.632 LF 0.699 0.698 IF 0.721 0.720 HF 0.723 0.721\n======================\n\n\n=== [BẢNG SỐ LIỆU] ===\nMô hình Accuracy Image 0.576 Text 0.667 LF 0.674 IF 0.678 HF 0.676 F1-score 0.566 0.633 0.625 0.649 0.634\n======================\nMVSA-Single\nMVSA-Multiple\n• Proposed 3 fusion models for Sentiment Analysis on Text & Image\n• Do experiments on many pre-trained CNN models to extract image features and DenseNet201 is the best result.\n• Enhanced features integrated on BERT didn’t improve the results.\n• Combine BERT+DenseNet201 and Hybrid Fusion and this is the best model on fusion approach.\nFuture direction\n• Focus more on data connection techniques at the feature level (intermediate fusion).\n• Apply attention mechanisms to the extracted feature for both text and image data.\n• Learn more about better ways to deal with imbalanced labels.\nThank you!\nDr. Bui Thanh Hung\nData Science Laboratory\nData Science Department, Faculty of Information Technology Industrial University of Ho Chi Minh city\nEmail: buithanhhung@iuh.edu.vn\nSite: https://sites.google.com/site/hungthanhbui1980\n	sentiment-analysis multimodal image text fusion	http://localhost:8888/api/v1/resource/download/asset/451e1192-5009-4f93-b756-244ff831d815.png
a2e03eb7-10e7-4b76-8a02-520616f290a2.pdf	Tài liệu này giới thiệu về học máy, tập trung vào các khái niệm và thuật toán cơ bản. Nó giải thích về các vấn đề học tập, bao gồm việc xây dựng các chương trình tự động cải thiện từ kinh nghiệm. Các phương pháp như FIND-S và Candidate-Elimination được thảo luận, cùng với các khái niệm về bias và overfitting.	application/pdf	0	t	This document delves into the realm of Machine Learning, exploring various concepts. It covers learning methodologies, including supervised and unsupervised learning, and delves into Concept Learning, hypothesis representation, and the FIND-S algorithm. Furthermore, it discusses the List-then-Eliminate and Candidate-Elimination algorithms, highlighting the significance of inductive bias and its impact on hypothesis spaces. The document touches upon decision trees, entropy, and information gain before concluding with discussions of overfitting and different types of bias.	5dddbe47-f8dc-4d8e-83e6-e848a9d90a26		Bach khoa University	[0.017062584,0.057813745,-0.010875432,0.034317713,0.035184793,-0.08675316,-0.014897361,-0.021798942,0.04820537,0.020290457,0.0010960258,0.004587719,0.11845769,0.062258072,-0.029188013,-0.060905345,0.013222789,-0.01446261,0.04876737,-0.016725447,0.04581702,-0.029808035,0.0003172981,-0.032124545,0.013741129,-0.027346846,0.03435535,0.017370135,-0.028740494,0.053341854,0.046678506,-0.018794898,0.030434757,0.012723991,0.03158452,0.0018460924,0.0036176818,-0.03004562,-0.021766704,0.043646127,0.015938787,0.010663255,0.03116171,-0.048783407,0.01658297,-0.01823406,0.016962748,-0.014581548,0.0030343034,-0.03450028,0.040252715,0.017838096,0.042294685,0.04387289,-0.054505356,-0.025383836,-0.010753364,0.018192383,-0.015820514,0.027920539,-0.005541231,0.03593185,-0.00015855233,0.05089069,0.055086646,-0.04274115,0.009655012,-0.04989145,-0.018553182,-0.02097675,0.016476365,-0.04406906,0.05169248,-0.05256336,-0.031122494,-0.0025661897,-0.032179855,0.021309314,-0.0010874042,-0.0077600125,0.0418