 regression\n3\n=a\nKy\n*3\no >0 > g\nW ==\ndx\n¥\nZ=Ww x+b\n= Q.-\ndo. —\nVI S —_— o2 2a z e\ndo\n=q®\nCircuit theory and deep learning\nInformally: There are functions you can compute with a small” L-layer deep neural network that shallower networks require exponentially more hidden units to compute\nForward and backward functions\nWhat are hyperparameters?\nParameters:\nW plil w2l pl2l 81 pl3l\nN~\nApplied deep learning is a very empirical process\nWord Embedding\nTo compare pieces of text\n• We need effective representation of :\n– Words\n– Sentences\n– Text\n• Approach 1: Use existing thesauri or ontologies like WordNet and Snomed CT (for medical). Drawbacks:\n– Manual\n– Not context specific\n• Approach 2: Use co-occurrences for word similarity. Drawbacks:\n– Quadratic space needed\n– Relative position and order of words not considered\nApproach 3: low dimensional vectors\n• Store only “important” information in fixed, low dimensional vector.\n• Single Value Decomposition (SVD) on co-occurrence matrix\n– is the best rank k approximation to X , in terms of least squares\n– Motel = [0.286, 0.792, -0.177, -0.107, 0.109, -0.542, 0.349, 0.271]\n• m = n = size of vocabulary\nProblems with SVD\n• Computational cost scales quadratically for n x m matrix: O(mn2) flops (when n<m)\n• Hard to incorporate new words or documents\n• Does not consider order of words\nword2vec Approach to represent the meaning of word\n• Represent each word with a low-dimensional vector\n• Word similarity = vector similarity\n• Key idea: Predict surrounding words of every word\n• Faster and can easily incorporate a new sentence/document or add a word to the vocabulary\nWord2Vec\nWord2Vec\nWord2Vec\nAuto-Encoder\nStacked Auto-Encoder\nWord2vec\nRepresent the meaning of word – word2vec\n• 2 basic neural network models:\n– Continuous Bag of Word (CBOW): use a window of word to predict the middle word\n– Skip-gram (SG): use a word to predict the surrounding ones in window.\nWord2vec – Continuous Bag of Word\n• E.g. “The cat sat on floor”\n– Window size = 2\nWe can consider either W or W’ as the word’s representation. Or even take the average.\nSome interesting results\nWord Analogies\nTest for linear relationships, examined by Mikolov et al. (2014)\n—\nman:woman :: king:?\nking [0.300.70] 0.75\nman [0.200.20]\nwoman [0.600.30]\nqueen [0.700.80]\nWord analogies\nCombination of tf.idf and WE\n• Recall\n•\n•\n	deep-learning natural-language-processing word-embedding neural-networks cbow	http://localhost:8888/api/v1/resource/download/asset/b029dc25-b4c1-489e-a63a-47b087dbb210.png
979bfb27-ce06-4733-9098-9006e043747e.pdf	Tài liệu này tập trung vào sự không chắc chắn trong trí tuệ nhân tạo, bao gồm xác suất, mạng Bayesian và logic mờ. Nó trình bày các khái niệm xác suất, bao gồm xác suất tiên nghiệm và có điều kiện. Ngoài ra, tài liệu thảo luận về mạng Bayesian, cú pháp, ngữ nghĩa và ứng dụng của chúng trong việc trả lời câu hỏi không chắc chắn. Cuối cùng, nó giới thiệu khái niệm tập mờ, định nghĩa và ứng dụng của chúng.	application/pdf	0	t	The document explores concepts in uncertain reasoning, covering probability theory, Bayesian networks, and fuzzy logic. It details probability concepts like conditional probability and Bayes' theorem. Bayesian Networks, their syntax, semantics and applications in uncertain question answering are discussed. The document then shifts to fuzzy logic, outlining fuzzy sets, operations, and applications in fuzzy control systems.	04069469-5a03-4cea-ab30-bead97dc4c85		Bach khoa University	[0.010763017,0.038696162,-0.0019023522,0.010047722,0.037694898,-0.08264836,-0.04784931,-0.02667674,0.044622023,0.043639105,0.007859643,0.008922186,0.12075508,0.03813606,-0.04362275,-0.051429246,0.017658917,-0.011348352,0.025663363,-0.014019008,0.0312123,-0.021839418,0.032980498,-0.02794813,0.010944143,-0.020859871,0.034764357,0.008604899,-0.009650246,0.065382935,0.055877604,-0.010625061,0.021530058,0.041842815,0.04257748,0.008758154,0.010414923,-0.024034807,0.028667869,0.02143995,0.009404891,0.032740995,0.008218925,-0.063898966,0.0362186,-0.014141202,0.007647355,0.006930881,-0.008871525,-0.033721425,0.05013988,-0.0049569756,0.011441182,0.0077473638,-0.035923902,-0.028099103,0.0077026426,0.036716044,-0.02039655,0.049082592,-0.03930806,0.011570029,0.0018390116,-0.0031895854,0.03157287,-0.025465399,0.013389415,-0.015362949,-0.013175116,-0.015778119,0.021822574,-0.00082777994,0.08034987,-0.053081874,-0.026585959,-0.019659888,-0.045482736,0.044906124,0.007939604,-0.021874016,0.04378232,0.030536372,0.010498002,0.040181756,0.04135406,0.00